// Real tenant notes, copied verbatim (LVX192 Task 5). Not secret.
export const HAMMERSLEYS_NOTES = "FIRST: if the caller needs a car now (now, ASAP, within about 30 minutes, or already waiting), skip the questions below: ask in one question for their name, where they are and where to, save it with the message beginning URGENT and the labels Where and Where to, then say you are putting them through to the dispatcher and use request_transfer.\nOtherwise ask their name first (if the trip is for someone else, also that person's name, label Passenger) and save straight away: caller_name and the reason as the message (Taxi booking request unless it is a cancel or change, complaint, lost property, driver job or account).\nFor a taxi request ask these one at a time with the short label shown. After EVERY answer, save again with caller_name, the same message and all the details so far. If an answer makes no sense or you did not catch it, ask again once. If they do not know something, skip it and never insist:\n1. Pickup: house number, street, village and postcode. Read it all back and ask if it is right.\n2. Destination: address and postcode, or airport and terminal (Gatwick: North or South). For an airport, also ask the flight number and time, label Flight.\n3. When: ask which DAY and the time to pick them up. A flight time is not a pick-up time.\n4. Passengers: how many. Needs: wheelchair, child seat (ask each child's age), 8-seater, female driver, dog (label Needs).\n5. Luggage: number of cases. More than 8 passengers or 8 cases: say the dispatcher will confirm.\n6. Payment: cash, card or account, and the account name.\nCancel or change a booking: you cannot change bookings. Take the booking's pick-up time and address and what to change (labels Booking and Change), save it, and say the dispatcher will confirm. Never say it is cancelled or changed. If the pick-up is within the next hour, also put them through.\nFor a complaint use the labels Trip date and What happened. For lost property use Item, Trip date and Trip details.";
export const DIGILE_NOTES = "Only for a new business enquiry; never ask these of an existing client, a personal caller, a supplier or a sales pitch.\nTake the message first as usual: name, number and reason, and save it with record_customer_request. Then ask these one at a time, saving the answers in details as you go, and skip anything they would rather not answer:\n1. Their company.\n2. Their industry.\n3. What they sell.\n4. The main thing holding back the growth of their business right now.\n5. Their email address. Ask them to spell it, and save what you heard.\n6. Roughly what they spend, or would like to spend, on marketing each month.\nThen ask which day and time suit them for a free consultation, save it as the preferred time, and say Ilija will be in touch to confirm. Nobody is turned away because of budget.";
